# Security Labs Documentation Rule

When the user says **"apply the new documentation rule file"** (or similar, e.g. "apply security_doc.mdc to tryhackme.md"), perform the documentation workflow below.

## Workflow Steps

1. **Read** `rough.md` for the raw content.
2. **Read** `format.md` and `old.md` for the template structure.
3. **Analyze** the rough content and map it to the format structure:
   - Introduction
   - Detailed Explanation (with `- [x]` checkboxes and sub-items)
   - Terminal Commands (fenced `bash` blocks with explanations)
   - Code (fenced code blocks with explanations)
   - Questions and Answers (10–20 Q&A in nested `<details><summary>Answer</summary>`; see bullet rule below)
   - Summary
   - References
4. **Generate** 10–20 revision Q&A from the content to aid study.
5. **Append** (do not overwrite) the formatted content to `tryhackme.md` even if the formatted content currently exists in tryhackme.md.

## Format Requirements

- Use HTML `<details>` and `<summary>` for accordion-style sections as defined in `format.md`.
- **Accordion spacing:** For every `<details>` block, put **one blank line** after the closing `</summary>` tag and **one blank line** before `</details>`, so the inner content is visually separated from the tags (same pattern as `format.md`). This applies to **topic** accordions (e.g. `<summary>Room Title</summary>`) and to **Q&A** accordions (`<summary>Answer</summary>`).
- Title for the accordion comes from the first `#` heading in `rough.md`.
- First reference in References must be the TryHackMe/Let's Defend page link (pasted at top of `rough.md`).
- Every other links should also be added under the reference section after the TryHackMe/Let's Defend page link.
- Each Q&A uses nested `<details><summary>Answer</summary>` with the answer inside, with blank lines after `</summary>` and before `</details>` as in **Accordion spacing** above.
- **Answer formatting:** Inside `<details><summary>Answer</summary>`, use **checked task-list lines** (`- [x] …`) for every answer line—whether there is **one** fact or **many** (e.g. a single header name, URL parts, record types, steps, flags, or “A vs B” lines). Do **not** use plain `- ` without `[x]` in Q&A answers. For multiple items, put **one `- [x]` line per item**, not one long comma-separated sentence.

## Content Guidelines

- For **Questions and Answers**, always format the answer body with **`- [x]`** lines inside `<details>` (same rule as Format Requirements above), not bare paragraphs or plain `-` bullets.
- One topic per accordion.
- Preserve all explanations, terminal commands, and code from the rough content.
- Use checkboxes (`- [x]`) for breakdown items in Detailed Explanation.
- Include sub-items where appropriate.
- If a section has no content (e.g. no code), omit it or leave a brief placeholder.

## File Paths

| Purpose                | Path           |
| ---------------------- | -------------- |
| Input (raw paste)      | `rough.md`     |
| Template               | `format.md`    |
| Output (append target) | `tryhackme.md` |
